<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB unit buys electrical firm.</title>
<headline>ABB unit buys electrical firm.</headline>
<dateline>BADEN, Switzerland 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABB Schweiz, a unit of the electriccal engineering group ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG, said it was acquiring the main businesses of the electrical installation firm Grossbacher-Gruppe.</p>
<p>The acquisition, which takes effect on July 1, covers Grossbacher companies in St.Gallen, Zurich and Biel, Switzerland, ABB said.</p>
<p>It said the three companies being acquired together employ about 520 workers and have a turnover of about 60 million Swiss francs. -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
